#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:111
msgid ""
"E-waste is [considered](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-new-circular-"
"vision-for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) the “fastest-growing waste "
"stream in the world”, with 44.7 million metric tons generated in 2016&mdash;"
"equivalent to [4,500 Eiffel Towers](https://www.itu.int/en/ITU-D/Climate-"
"Change/Documents/GEM%202017/Global-E-waste%20Monitor%202017%20.pdf), which, "
"when stacked, is 17 times higher than Mount Everest. In 2018, an estimated "
"50 million metric tons of e-waste was reported, motivating the UN to refer "
"to a “[tsunami of e-waste](https://news.un.org/en/story/2015/05/497772) "
"rolling out over the world”. The numbers continue to rise: in 2021, an "
"estimated [57 million metric tons](https://www.bbc.com/news/science-"
"environment-61350996) of e-waste was generated globally. [Less than 20 "
"percent](https://weee-forum.org/ws_news/international-e-waste-day-2021/) of "
"it is collected and recycled, and although it makes up [only 2%](https://www."
"forbes.com/sites/vianneyvaute/2019/04/23/with-love-from-an-oregon-prison-how-"
"eric-lundgren-is-going-to-help-you-recycle-all-your-electronics/) of trash "
"in landfills, it contributes to almost 70% of the toxic waste found there."
msgstr ""
"O lixo eletrônico é [considerado](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-new-"
"circular-vision-for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) o “fluxo de "
"resíduos que cresce mais rapidamente no mundo“, com 44,7 milhões de "
"toneladas métricas geradas em 2016 &mdash; o equivalente a [4.500 Torres "
"Eiffel](https://www.itu.int/en/ITU-D/Climate-Change/Documents/GEM%202017/"
"Global-E-waste%20Monitor%202017%20.pdf), que, quando empilhadas, são 17 "
"vezes mais altas que o Monte Everest. Em 2018, foram estimadas 50 milhões de "
"toneladas métricas de lixo eletrônico, o que levou a ONU a se referir a um "
"“[tsunami de lixo eletrônico](https://news.un.org/en/story/2015/05/497772) "
"se espalhando pelo mundo”. Os números continuam a subir: em 2021, foram "
"geradas estimadas [57 milhões de toneladas métricas](https://www.bbc.com/"
"news/science-environment-61350996) de lixo eletrônico em todo o mundo. "
"[Menos de 20%](https://weee-forum.org/ws_news/international-e-waste-"
"day-2021/) dele é coletado e reciclado, e embora represente [apenas 2%]"
"(https://www.forbes.com/sites/vianneyvaute/2019/04/23/with-love-from-an-"
"oregon-prison-how-eric-lundgren-is-going-to-help-you-recycle-all-your-"
"electronics/) do lixo em aterros sanitários, contribui com quase 70% dos "
"resíduos tóxicos encontrados lá."

